# The workspace-inspection records of the binary decomposition tree and the
# Agent-CLI ladder that executes it: the tree invariants (two children per
# internal node, atomic leaves, dotted child paths, 63 nodes at depth five) and
# the ladder facts (leaf-first order, fresh repository copies, exact node-path
# proofs). Each surface names a fact a request asks about; its `action` is the
# literal or the source pattern the repository search looks for. Moved out of
# meanings-coding-tasks.lino (PR #1188).
meanings
  binary_decomposition_invariant
    defined-by code
    role coding_search_literal_query
    precondition "a workspace-inspection request plainly states the binary decomposition invariant"
    effect "the repository-search subject is bound to the binary decomposition invariant"
    unit "not applicable"
    example "internal node has exactly two children"
    lexeme en "internal node has exactly two children" "internal nodes have exactly two children"
      action binary_decomposition_invariant
    lexeme ru "внутренний узел имеет ровно двух потомков"
      action binary_decomposition_invariant
    lexeme hi "आंतरिक नोड के ठीक दो बच्चे होते हैं"
      action binary_decomposition_invariant
    lexeme zh 内部节点恰好有两个子节点
      action binary_decomposition_invariant
    lexeme es "un nodo interno tiene exactamente dos hijos"
      action binary_decomposition_invariant
